From cd42449a85f905cc061f75e72adb41558bc5c646 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:51:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pivot: reframe AEGIS as an exposure-and-coverage evidence
 mapper

Course review feedback flagged the original problem statement: it
understated Qusar's existing agent-level governance and combined
governance with an unvalidated insurance product (no coverage
definitions, claims data, actuarial methodology, or legal scope),
making the pitch neither differentiated nor feasible.

Per the reviewer's suggested reframe, AEGIS now consumes decision
evidence, identifies missing controls, maps decisions to broad
insurance exposure categories, and exports audit evidence --
explicitly dropping anything that reads as a real payout trigger,
a premium/pricing decision, or a compliance certification:

- com.aegis.payout -> com.aegis.evidence. PayoutEngineService ->
  EvidenceMappingService: no more $ amounts or "SLA breach payout";
  a flagged or unreviewed decision now produces an EvidenceRecord
  tagged with an exposure category (Underwriting Risk / Claims
  Handling / Fraud & Integrity Exposure) and a control-gap flag.
- PricingFeedbackService -> ExposureAggregationService: no more
  premium multiplier. Tracks an informational evidence rate and
  dominant exposure category per agent -- explicitly never a
  premium, coverage term, or compliance certification.
- PayoutResult contract -> ExposureEvidenceRecord.
- New GET /api/evidence/export: a downloadable JSON audit bundle --
  the actual "export audit evidence" deliverable the reviewer asked
  for, not previously built.
- Dashboard, evidence/records.html (was payout/payouts.html), and
  nav updated to match -- including an explicit on-page scope
  banner ("AEGIS does not certify compliance, make a legal coverage
  determination, or set a premium").
- README, package READMEs, CLAUDE_PROMPTS.md, and CONTRIBUTING.md
  updated: revised problem statement, proposed solution, and
  architecture description; Person C's prompt rewritten for the
  evidence package.
- Tests renamed and rewritten to match (EvidenceMappingServiceTest,
  ExposureAggregationServiceTest).

Not run through `mvn test` in this environment -- Maven Central is
blocked by this sandbox's egress policy. Did a full manual
cross-check of every renamed type, constructor, field, and template
binding instead; please run the suite locally before merging.

